1
00:00:00,091 --> 00:00:03,174
Welcome to the 6F's protocol mastery practice.

2
00:00:03,734 --> 00:00:07,297
This practice guides you through six steps for getting to know a part.

3
00:00:08,018 --> 00:00:14,183
Find, focus, flesh out, feel toward, befriend, and fear.

4
00:00:15,184 --> 00:00:15,945
Move slowly.

5
00:00:16,946 --> 00:00:19,288
You do not have to complete every step perfectly.

6
00:00:19,888 --> 00:00:22,110
Begin by settling into your body.

7
00:00:23,111 --> 00:00:24,252
Take a slow breath in.

8
00:00:34,418 --> 00:00:35,120
and let it out.

9
00:00:36,804 --> 00:00:38,328
The first step is find.

10
00:00:39,411 --> 00:00:40,273
Ask inside.

11
00:00:41,175 --> 00:00:43,682
What part of me is asking for attention right now?

12
00:00:57,017 --> 00:00:57,838
Notice one part.

13
00:00:58,759 --> 00:01:05,644
It might appear as a body sensation, emotion, thought, image, impulse, or memory.

14
00:01:06,505 --> 00:01:08,767
The second step is focus.

15
00:01:09,968 --> 00:01:11,869
Bring gentle attention to this part.

16
00:01:12,910 --> 00:01:17,914
Not too close, not too far, just enough to notice it.

17
00:01:19,356 --> 00:01:23,479
Ask, where do I sense this part in or around my body?

18
00:01:36,663 --> 00:01:38,446
The third step is flesh out.

19
00:01:39,467 --> 00:01:40,709
Notice more about the part.

20
00:01:41,631 --> 00:01:42,612
Does it have an image?

21
00:01:43,374 --> 00:01:43,814
A shape?

22
00:01:44,696 --> 00:01:45,136
A color?

23
00:01:46,118 --> 00:01:46,659
An age?

24
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:48,181
A posture?

25
00:01:49,203 --> 00:01:49,703
A voice?

26
00:01:50,805 --> 00:01:51,286
A feeling?

27
00:02:04,240 --> 00:02:06,642
Let it become more known without forcing.

28
00:02:07,683 --> 00:02:09,525
The fourth step is feel toward.

29
00:02:10,706 --> 00:02:14,190
Ask, how do I feel toward this part?

30
00:02:27,767 --> 00:02:31,030
If you feel curious, compassionate, or calm, notice that.

31
00:02:31,951 --> 00:02:38,938
If you feel angry, afraid, ashamed, annoyed, or numb, that may be another part.

32
00:02:40,279 --> 00:02:43,943
Ask that reacting part if it can give you a little space.

33
00:02:57,470 --> 00:02:59,451
Now return to the original part.

34
00:03:00,592 --> 00:03:02,253
The fifth step is befriend.

35
00:03:03,273 --> 00:03:05,974
Let the part know you are not here to get rid of it.

36
00:03:06,995 --> 00:03:10,417
You might say, I want to understand you.

37
00:03:11,537 --> 00:03:13,959
I know you may be trying to help.

38
00:03:15,279 --> 00:03:16,600
I am willing to listen.

39
00:03:36,136 --> 00:03:38,317
Ask, what do you want me to know?

40
00:03:51,562 --> 00:03:51,862
Listen.

41
00:04:11,107 --> 00:04:12,789
The sixth step is fear.

42
00:04:14,051 --> 00:04:14,872
Ask the part.

43
00:04:16,114 --> 00:04:19,398
What are you afraid would happen if you did not do your job?

44
00:04:32,460 --> 00:04:33,541
Listen gently.

45
00:04:34,582 --> 00:04:37,886
This question often reveals what the part is protecting.

46
00:04:38,987 --> 00:04:39,968
Now thank the part.

47
00:04:40,729 --> 00:04:42,410
You do not have to solve everything.

48
00:04:43,512 --> 00:04:44,673
You have practiced listening.

49
00:04:46,014 --> 00:04:49,638
Ask, what would help you trust me a little more next time?

50
00:05:03,192 --> 00:05:03,552
Listen.

51
00:05:22,587 --> 00:05:24,408
Now take a slow breath in.

52
00:05:34,104 --> 00:05:34,866
and let it out.

53
00:05:35,868 --> 00:05:36,890
Return to the room.

54
00:05:46,849 --> 00:05:50,817
Remember, mastery does not mean rushing through the steps.

55
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:55,947
Mastery means returning with patience, respect, and self-energy.
